    <h2 class="article-title">Of Salvation</h2>
    <div class="article-body">
        <p><strong>We believe</strong> that <span data-span="s1" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Jesus Christ offers entrance to the Kingdom of God through His Gospel of Salvation</span>. We seek to understand <span data-span="s2" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">what we are being saved from and what we are being saved for—though we may never fully comprehend these things in mortality</span>, for <span data-span="s3" data-article="A06" data-type="direct" data-named="false">"Eye hath not seen, nor ear heard, neither have entered into the heart of man, the things which God hath prepared for them that love him."</span></p>
        <p><span data-span="s4" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Salvation from our sins and mortality, through the grace and Atonement of the Son of God</span>, <span data-span="s5" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">stands at the center of the grand arc of God's Plan</span>: <span data-span="s6" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">from our creation in His image, through redemptive transformation, to the day that we receive His image in our countenance</span> and <span data-span="s7" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">become like Him—flourishing and glorified together as co-heirs with Christ of the Kingdom of God</span>.</p>
        <p>As followers of Christ, we <span data-span="s16" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">invite the Holy Spirit while searching the scriptures</span>, <span data-span="s17" data-article="A06" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">leaning not to our own understanding and trusting not in the arm of flesh</span>. We heed <span data-span="s18" data-article="A06" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">Paul's counsel to work out our own salvation with fear and trembling before the Lord</span>.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s8" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We do not claim to know the full eternal mechanisms by which salvation in Christ operates</span>, <span data-span="s9" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">nor do we dare to reduce it to any single aspect of the whole Gospel that Jesus Christ taught plainly</span>: <span data-span="s10" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">justice, mercy, grace, and Atonement freely offered in Him; faith in God and belief in His Son, prayer and repentance by which we turn to Him</span>; <span data-span="s11" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the new birth; and the love, forgiveness, peace, humility, patience, gentleness, and kindness by which His life grows whole within us</span>. <span data-span="s12" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Nor do we overlook obedience, discipleship, perseverance, and good works that bear fruit to His glory</span>, or <span data-span="s13" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the joy, sanctification, and sealing by the Holy Spirit that open unto resurrection, immortality, eternal life, and glorification</span>.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s14" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We claim no right to sit upon the throne of Christ, judging no soul to be saved or condemned in His place</span>. <span data-span="s15" data-article="A06" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Rather, we remember our charge before Him: to love God and neighbor without ceasing, to profess our faith in Him, and to keep His commandments</span>.</p>
